PHASE 3 — PARTITIONED SEATING ENGINE — IMPLEMENTATION VERIFICATION RECORD
(Evidence-only inspection of the committed implementation at 0583fb0 / HEAD 82670fc.
Read-only: no code was modified during this close-out.)

PHASE A — Physical interaction graph (solver-service/app/graph.py)
- PhysicalSeatGraph.build(halls, adjacency=eight|cardinal): nodes built sorted by
  (hallNumber, row, column); seat geometry validated (row letter within rows grid,
  column within columns grid -> ValueError on out-of-grid seats).
- Horizontal adjacency: (dr==0, dc==1). Vertical: (dr==1, dc==0).
  Eight (default): max(dr,dc)==1 (Chebyshev 1, same hall). Cardinal: cardinal
  only. Lines 103-105.
- Hall isolation: cross-hall edges detected (cross_hall_edges); build rejects any
  cross-hall edge unless allow_cross_hall_adjacency=True; isolation_errors() lists
  them. No cross-hall edges are produced by the default same-hall rule.
- Unknown adjacency mode -> ValueError.

PHASE B — Domain partitioning (solver-service/app/partition.py)
- _UnionFind with find (path-halving) + union (lines 52-62); connected components
  computed from graph edges (lines 75+). Each component is one Domain (domain_id,
  seat_indices, hall_ids, building_ids, candidate_ids).
- verify_partition_invariants() checks: every seat in exactly one domain, every
  seat present, and no adjacency edge crosses domains (lines 108+).
- allocate_candidates_to_domains: deterministic balanced round-robin per department
  (respects seat capacity); used by tests/benchmarks; deployment allocation is the
  orchestrator's job per §11.1.
- Ceiling: MAX_DOMAIN_CANDIDATES_DEFAULT = 1000; partition_request flags any domain
  with candidate_count > ceiling as oversized with
  ERR_GRAPH_TOPOLOGY_OVERSIZED_COMPONENT (solver not invoked).
- topology_anomaly_evidence(): structured evidence (candidate_count, seat_count,
  ceiling, hall_ids, adjacency edges within the domain) for oversized domains.

GUARDS (solver-service/app/guards.py)
- compute_composition_report -> CompositionReport with classification in
  {BALANCED, IMBALANCE_RISK, INSUFFICIENT_CAPACITY}.
- INSUFFICIENT_CAPACITY only when candidate_count > seat_count
  (ERR_INSUFFICIENT_DOMAIN_CAPACITY) - a real capacity error, NOT a composition risk.
- IMBALANCE_RISK is a pre-dispatch scheduling-risk classification produced by
  configurable CompositionLimits ratios (largestDepartmentRatio / largestYearRatio /
  largestCohortRatio / maxEmptySeatRatio). Ratios are risk thresholds, NOT
  mathematical infeasibility proofs (owner correction 2026-08-15). Year/cohort risk
  flagged only when >=2 distinct buckets exist (len(...) >= 2 guard, line 101).
- compositionAction: warn (default) or reject -> ERR_DOMAIN_COMPOSITION_IMBALANCE.

PHASE C — Seat-label channeling solver (solver-service/app/seatlabel.py)
- X[c,s]: NewBoolVar X_{s}_{ci} (line 89). O[s]: occupancy bool (line 91).
  D[s]/Y[s]/K[s]: NewIntVar over 0..len, index 0 = EMPTY sentinel (lines 92-99).
  K only created when cohorts present (policy COHORT), Y only when years present -
  K/Y are "only where required".
- Channeling by linear weighted sums: D[s] == sum_c X[c,s]*deptIndex(c); same for
  Y/K. EMPTY (all X=0) => label 0.
- One seat per candidate: sum_s X[c,s] == 1 for every domain candidate (line 111);
  one candidate per seat: sum_c X[c,s] <= 1; O[s] == sum_c X[c,s].
- Anti-adjacency reified ON OCCUPANCY (OnlyEnforceIf([O[i],O[j]]), never blind
  label inequality): DEPARTMENT_ONLY => D[i]!=D[j]; STRICT_DEPT_OR_YEAR =>
  D[i]!=D[j] AND Y[i]!=Y[j]; COHORT => K[i]!=K[j] (lines 138-143).
- Policy modes from SolverConfig.policyMode (DEPARTMENT_ONLY default).
- Objective: minimize adjacent OCCUPIED same-department pairs (soft; forced 0 under
  DEPARTMENT_ONLY / STRICT_DEPT_OR_YEAR).
- Objective reporting (§18): OPTIMAL reports int(round(solver.ObjectiveValue())) and
  MUST equal validator sameDepartmentAdjacentCount, else ERR_VALIDATOR_MISMATCH
  (lines 388-397); FEASIBLE reports the validator-derived value.
- Validator mismatch handling: ERR_VALIDATOR_MISMATCH (reported != validator),
  ERR_INVALID_ASSIGNMENT (duplicate candidate/seat or policy violation).
- Policy requiring year without year present -> ERR_INVALID_POLICY_CONFIGURATION.
- Ceiling enforced before CP-SAT: oversized domain -> ERR_GRAPH_TOPOLOGY_OVERSIZED_COMPONENT
  (lines 463, 517, 612). Composition guard: INSUFFICIENT_CAPACITY -> INFEASIBLE
  (ERR_INSUFFICIENT_DOMAIN_CAPACITY); IMBALANCE_RISK + reject -> ERROR
  (ERR_DOMAIN_COMPOSITION_IMBALANCE).

VERIFICATION SUMMARY: all Phase A-C architecture elements claimed in the milestone
report are present in the committed implementation. No discrepancies found in this
inspection.